\begin{itemize}
    \item Hydropower and Others have positive CIs entirely above zero.
    \item Banking’s interval straddles zero – not statistically significant.
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Robust ANOVA and Permutation Test}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Robust ANOVA (20\% trimmed means):} \(F_t = 12.2519\), \(p < 0.001\), effect size \(\eta = 0.16\) (moderate-to-large).
    \item Confirms month effect is not driven by outliers.
    \item \textbf{Permutation test:} \(p < 2.2\times10^{-16}\) – strongest distribution-free evidence of seasonality.
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Two-Way Interaction ANOVA}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Sector:} \(F=0.502\), \(p=0.775\) – not significant.
    \item \textbf{Month:} \(F=10.44\), \(p<2\times10^{-16}\) – highly significant.
    \item \textbf{Sector×Month interaction:} \(F=0.702\), \(p=0.954\) – not significant.
\end{itemize}
\begin{itemize}
    \item The seasonal pattern is uniform across sectors.
    \item A single seasonal calendar applies broadly; only minor sector-specific adjustments (e.g., later exit for Hydropower) are needed.
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Summary of Key Findings}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{July (Shrawan) is the best month:} highest returns, win ratios \(>60\%\), perfect consistency for Banking.
    \item \textbf{August–September are worst:} negative returns, low win ratios, negative Sharpe ratios.
    \item \textbf{Optimal exit:} late July to early August (day 210–213) for most sectors; Hydropower later (day 230).
    \item \textbf{Z-score signals:} average entry Z ~ -2.0; threshold of \(\pm 1.8\) reduces false signals.
    \item \textbf{Reliable months:} July, January, November are consistently positive across years.
    \item \textbf{Sector uniformity:} seasonal pattern is common across sectors; unified strategy works.
\end{itemize}
\end{frame}

% ------------------- SECTION: Conclusion -------------------
\section{Conclusion}

\begin{frame}{Conclusion}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Strong monthly seasonality} confirmed by multiple tests (\(p<0.001\)).
    \item \textbf{July is the optimal entry month} – highest mean returns, win ratios, and consistency.
    \item \textbf{August–September are avoidance windows} – uniformly negative returns.
    \item \textbf{Optimal exit:} late July–early August; Hydropower later, Manufacturing requires caution.
    \item \textbf{Z-score framework} provides actionable signals; a conservative threshold is recommended.
    \item \textbf{Sector-invariant pattern} – a single seasonal calendar works for all sectors.
\end{enumerate}
\begin{block}{Practical Implication}
These findings challenge weak-form efficiency and provide evidence-based timing rules for NEPSE investors.
\end{block}
\end{frame}

